{%- comment -%}
  Keeps the guide page out of search engines (the original static site did the
  same with a meta tag, robots.txt and a response header).

  Add this ONE line inside <head> in layout/theme.liquid:

    {% render 'guide-noindex' %}

  It only does anything on pages that use the "jrtrack-guide" page template, so
  it is safe to leave in. Delete the snippet or the line if you want the guide
  to be indexed.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if template.name == 'page' and template.suffix == 'jrtrack-pro-user-guide' -%}
  <meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow">
{%- endif -%}
